---
import { projects } from "../data/projects";
import ProjectCard from "./ProjectCard.astro";
import BidPipelineDiagram from "./BidPipelineDiagram.astro";
---

<section
  id="projects"
  aria-labelledby="projects-heading"
  class="border-y border-border bg-band"
>
  <div class="page-shell py-14 md:py-20">
    <div aria-hidden="true" class="h-0.5 w-8 rounded-full bg-accent"></div>
    <h2
      id="projects-heading"
      class="mt-4 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-heading"
    >
      Projects
    </h2>
    {/*
      Answers "why these projects" at the moment a reader is looking at them,
      rather than making them scroll to About for it. The longer personal
      version of the same answer lives in About; this is the version tied to
      the work itself.
    */}
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-muted">
      City planning decides who can reach what, and Seattle publishes the data
      behind those decisions. Publishing it is not the same as being able to ask
      it a question, which is what the energy agent is for. The two FCP Insight
      systems are the same instinct applied at work, where the data is private
      but the problem is identical.
    </p>

    {/*
      Spelled out rather than passing a conditional into the slot, because
      Astro.slots.has() reports true for a slot that was provided but rendered
      nothing, which would leave an empty visual strip on the other cards.
    */}
    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      {
        projects.map((project) =>
          project.slug === "bid-grading-system" ? (
            <ProjectCard project={project}>
              <BidPipelineDiagram slot="visual" />
            </ProjectCard>
          ) : (
            <ProjectCard project={project} />
          ),
        )
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
